{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3098","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3098","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3098\",\"parent_revision\":\"e4438cab51e045b735c977f5d359b1d561c404e2da45f25f1e09dfc17d8d2e43\",\"root_revision\":\"e4438cab51e045b735c977f5d359b1d561c404e2da45f25f1e09dfc17d8d2e43\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThis is an exploration/experiment item. The deliverable is an experiment result or design decision with evidence (a prototype on a real plan, a measured comparison, or a written design verdict) \u2014 not a mandate to ship the feature. Origin: comparison of graph-engineering research against the development-harness architecture, grounded against the #3060 agent over-orchestration incident (a task-worker recursively dispatched sub-teams after receiving orchestrator-voiced prose; ~$100 of unplanned spend). Shared design constraint across all seven exploration items in this set: the model keeps the judgment (scoring, declaring, deciding semantic dependencies) but writes it down ONCE, as typed data, at planning time; the mechanical consequence is applied deterministically by machinery that already exists (sam_schema models, DependencyGraph, the implement-feature dispatch loop, work-milestone). No new scheduler, no generic graph runtime \u2014 that larger direction is explicitly out of scope for these items.\\n\\nWhat/why: SAM task dependencies currently express eligibility only (\\\"T3 may start when T1 and T2 complete\\\"). The information a downstream task needs from upstream (files changed, artifacts produced, discoveries, contract changes) is relayed as improvised prose \u2014 the milestone discovery-relay pattern builds relay text by hand and injects it into next-wave prompts. Improvised prose transfer of structured facts is the same defect class that produced the #3060 over-orchestration incident (a hand-written delegation prompt carrying information that should have been structured): lossy, unvalidated, and each producer reinvents the format.\\n\\nMitigates: lossy/inconsistent upstream-to-downstream context transfer; downstream workers re-discovering what upstream already established; the prose-improvisation defect class.\\n\\nBenefit lands in: start-task (registers the payload at completion), the implement-feature dispatch loop and work-milestone relay (inject the payload verbatim instead of composing prose), and downstream task quality.\\n\\nProposed exploration: (1) define a Pydantic TaskHandoff model in sam_schema (files_changed, commits, artifacts, discoveries, contracts_changed); (2) start-task registers it when marking a task complete; (3) the dispatch loop injects the upstream handoffs of a task's dependencies into its dispatch prompt mechanically; (4) trial on one multi-task plan and compare downstream workers' re-discovery overhead (repeated reads/greps of ground upstream already covered) against a baseline plan.\\n\\nRelated: Item 5 (\\\"Explore readiness-based dispatch in work-milestone, replacing whole-wave barriers\\\") \u2014 the milestone relay is the wave-level instance of the same gap.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Experiment or design exploration executed as described (prototype on a real plan, measured comparison, or written design verdict)\\n- [ ] Decision recorded with evidence: adopt, adapt, or reject \u2014 with rationale\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **explore typed handoff payloads so task edges carry data flow, not just eligibility** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: graph-engineering research comparison\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"9efc11c0ce7669513e9295a9ffc2a7b7acc711891e9617d76dbba55645357dec\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIpKWQ\"}"}